  "coverageRule": {
    "kind": "exclusive_authoritative_provinces",
    "exceptions": [
      "Island societies without a single territorial state are represented as historically named political communities with distributed-council center exceptions, not fictitious borders.",
      "Small islands, atolls, clans, hapū, and local chiefdoms compressed by playable terrain remain authoritative in preservedEntities attached to the encompassing island-group province.",
      "Ocean corridors express voyaging reach and contact, not ownership of open water."
    ]
